# conclusion 
'''The given program calculates the factorial of a number using a recursive approach. The time complexity is O(n) because the function calls itself repeatedly from n down to 1, resulting in approximately n function calls. The space complexity is O(n) because each recursive function call is stored in the call stack until the base condition is reached. Therefore, the program takes O(n) time and O(n) space. In conclusion, recursion makes the factorial program simple and easy to understand, but it requires more memory compared to the iterative approach, which has O(1) space complexity.'''